body:
The reason why I added this test was to make sure that `unmount` is called in `dispose` in all cases because we return the state early.

For example, the test would fail if the implementation was like that:

```js
dispose({ state }) {
  if (Object.keys(trackedFilters).length > 0) {
    const reinitRuleContexts = state
      .getQueryParameter('ruleContexts')
      .filter((rule: string) => !addedRuleContexts.includes(rule));

    return state.setQueryParameter('ruleContexts', reinitRuleContexts);
  }

  // Does not get called because `trackedFilters` was defined.
  unmount();

  return state;
},
```

The test doesn't provide much value in itself. I wrote it because when refactoring the `dispose` function I saw some potential misbehaviors here.

I can remove it if it feels unnecessary.

